Refuse Vulkan work before allocation or transfer after device loss.

Selective backport from JamesQiu2005/SpektraLab Windows_Linux at
 a4289ab99bc09fc998e6148dc3d496f9079e5857 (2026-11-09).
Source: https://github.com/JamesQiu2005/SpektraLab/tree/a4289ab99bc09fc998e6148dc3d496f9079e5857

Extends Android patch 0008 while retaining pooled descriptors, mapped
inline arguments, pipeline cache, and bounded/small-buffer pool policies.
The queue-lock recheck precedes the Android inline-ring host copy. The
first diagnostic stays stable and retains the app's (VkResult -4) marker.
Cleanup remains available. No shader arithmetic or resource pin changes.

Includes upstream's safe latch-injection regression, extended to the
Android bounded allocator and every upload wrapper, plus its CMake target.
The regression links the production backend and does not cause a real GPU
reset. Also carries upstream's explicit pipeline <algorithm> include.

